    "content": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Multiplying integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Multiplying"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Work with distances first. Then decide the sign. Same signs give a positive result. Different signs give a negative result."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "(-6) x 4 = -24",
            "6 x (-4) = -24",
            "(-6) x (-4) = 24"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-2/sign-rules.png",
          "image_alt": "Sign rules chart for multiplication and division"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "More than two factors"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Count the negative factors. An even number of negatives gives a positive product. An odd number gives a negative product. Example: (-1) x (-2) x (-3) = -6."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "video_code": "VID-INTEGER-MULTIPLY-DIVIDE",
          "segment_start_seconds": 45,
          "segment_end_seconds": 90
        },
        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Choosing the sign",
          "problem": "Compute (-6) x 4.",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Signs of (-6) x 4 are different. Result is negative.",
            "Step 2: 6 x 4 = 24."
          ],
          "answer": "Answer: -24."
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "(-6) x 4 = 24 is wrong. The signs are different, so the answer is -24."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 2.2 - Multiplying integers\nSkill: S3\nObjective:\n1. Multiply integers.\nMultiplying\nWork with distances first. Then decide the sign.\nSame signs -> positive\nDifferent signs -> negative\nExamples: (-6) x 4 = -24. 6 x (-4) = -24. (-6) x (-4) = 24.\nMore than two factors\nCount the negative factors. An even number of negatives gives a positive product. An odd number gives a negative product.\nExample: (-1) x (-2) x (-3) = -6.\nWorked example\nProblem: Compute (-6) x 4.\nStep 1: Signs of (-6) x 4 are different. Result is negative. Step 2: 6 x 4 = 24. Answer: -24.\nCommon mistake\n(-6) x 4 = 24 is wrong. The signs are different, so the answer is -24."
    }
  },
